product-rotation realization","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:a4d717eb280591f7947abae062783fc4ece9c102dffee0f54d281fea25942c05","file":"preprints/Invariant-projection-counterexamples-for-every-irrational-rotation-September-27-2026/build/appendix-product.tex","line":27,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"ddc3512134715147f8f4bc6605d9c4b8855fb4ec5409fde42268d8cbe2120f0c","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Invariant-projection-counterexamples-for-every-irrational-rotation-September-27-2026/build/appendix-product.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a4d717eb280591f7947abae062783fc4ece9c102dffee0f54d281fea25942c05","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Invariant-projection-counterexamples-for-every-irrational-rotation-September-27-2026/build/appendix-product.tex#L27"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{p:thm:model}\nThere are angles $0<\\theta_i<1$ and costs $c_i>0$, with\n$\\sum_i\\theta_i<\\infty$ and $1,\\theta_1,\\theta_2,\\ldots$ rationally\nindependent, such that the measurable weight\n\\[\n f(x)=\\exp\\left(-\\sum_{i\\ge1}c_i\\lfloor x_i+\\theta_i\\rfloor\\right)\n\\]\nis positive almost everywhere and has $\\int_X\\log f\\,d\\mu=-\\infty$.\nThe algebra $M$ is a type $\\mathrm{II}_1$ factor with separable predual,\nand $T=U\\pi(f)$ is nonzero and norm-quasinilpotent, with\n$\\Delta(T)=0$.  Every projection $p\\in M$ satisfying $(1-p)Tp=0$ is\n$0$ or $1$.\n\nMoreover, $|T|$ has pure-point spectral type.  The abelian algebra\ngenerated by any finite family of polar conjugates\n$U^n|T|U^{-n}$ is atomic, whereas\n$W^*(U^n|T|U^{-n}:n\\in\\Z)$ is diffuse."}
